&lt;h3&gt;About the job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Turn product intent into the technical work that moves AI compute forward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Technical Product Owner, you will help component-based software teams deliver clear, prioritised and meaningful outcomes. You will connect product intent, engineering delivery and cross-team coordination.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your work will support software that spans bare metal silicon through to the machine learning tools stack. You will make complex systems easier to plan, explain and deliver.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own component backlogs, shape roadmaps, refine epics and stories, and support sprint and PI planning. You will also surface dependencies, risks and trade-offs early.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role suits someone who brings calm, clarity and momentum to technical teams. You will help engineers focus on the work that matters most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The team and culture&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work with component-based software teams across Graphcore’s engineering organisation. These teams build across the full AI compute stack, from silicon-level software to ML tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work happens through clear planning, practical discussion and fast feedback. You will help teams visualise progress, involve the right people and make delivery risks visible early.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Decisions are shaped by product outcomes, technical evidence and team insight. You will encourage open challenge, protect focus and enable empowered decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Experience working as a Product Owner, or in a similar agile role.&lt;br&gt;· Strong backlog management, refinement and roadmap development skills.&lt;br&gt;· Ability to communicate clearly with technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;br&gt;· Confidence working with technical teams, complex systems and cross-team dependencies.&lt;br&gt;· Strong facilitation skills, with the ability to guide discu

&lt;p&gt;Graphcore is a globally recognized leader in Artificial Intelligence computing systems. The company designs advanced semiconductors and datacentre hardware that provide the specialized processing power needed to drive AI innovation, while delivering the efficiency required to support its broader adoption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the SoftBank Group, Graphcore is a member of an elite family of companies responsible for some of the world’s most transformative technologies. Together, we are working to enable Artificial Super Intelligence and ensure that its benefits are accessible to everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are developing the next generation of AI compute, a large-scale system-on-chip (SoC) designed to power future high-performance AI systems. As the Director of Post Silicon Validation, you will be responsible for leading the Bristol team, enabling pre-production software to run reliably on new silicon quickly and efficiently, before showing that the silicon meets the highest standards of quality, reliability and functionality, ready for production deployment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Senior Director of Post Silicon Validation, you will manage, develop and grow the Post Silicon Validation team in Bristol, delivering post-silicon validation across the full AI SoC, working across silicon, firmware, and platform levels. The role requires a deep technical understanding, strong hands-on debug experience, and the ability to collaborate effectively with hardware, software, and systems engineering teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage, develop and grow the Post Silicon Validation team in Bristol: &lt;/strong&gt;The Post Silicon Validation team is relatively new, with a strong remit and growing quickly to help Graphcore bring up new silicon quickly and effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Play a significant role in the definition, planning and execut

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build the test strategy that protects Graphcore’s system software releases at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff System Software Engineer, you will shape integration and system testing across firmware, BMC and Linux device drivers. Your work will help create a high quality gate for system software release packages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will design, build, automate and report tests across complex server class systems. You will also develop reusable tools, pipelines and packaging solutions that help teams move faster with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role needs deep low level software knowledge and strong system thinking. You will own hard technical areas, guide best practice and stay close to the code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The team and culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join a new integration and system test team within System Software QA. The team verifies integrated components across BMC, firmware and Linux device drivers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work happens close to the hardware, across component teams and QA. You will partner with developers, consult package stakeholders and turn use cases into robust system tests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Decisions are shaped by evidence, clear technical reasoning and ownership. You will be expected to speak up, act fast and raise standards through hands-on leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Strong experience in low level system testing and integration across complex software and hardware layers.&lt;br&gt;· Deep understanding of RTOS, complex boot logic, Linux and device drivers.&lt;br&gt;· Test development capability using Python and C/C++.&lt;br&gt;· Experience working with hardware, debuggers, CI/CD pipelines and build or integration tools.&lt;br&gt;· Ability to debug cross-layer issues and drive root-cause investigations to lasting corrective actions.&lt;br&g

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the test strategy that proves Graphcore’s next generation drivers are production-ready.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff System Software Engineer, you will shape how Graphcore validates complex device drivers and platform tools. You will bring technical depth across Linux kernels, drivers and systems software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your work will help raise the quality bar for products that support the next generation of AI compute. You will influence design decisions, guide test infrastructure and drive reliability across the stack.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will design, build, execute and report tests across component, system and acceptance levels. You will debug difficult issues using hardware and software tools, simulators and emulators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on technical leadership role with broad reach. You will help teams move quickly while protecting production quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The team and culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Drivers QA team verifies low-level kernel drivers, user-space libraries and platform tools. Work spans component tests, user acceptance and full system validation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work directly with driver developers, hardware, firmware, ML stack, Kubernetes and cloud management teams. Decisions are made close to the technical detail, with engineers expected to speak up and own outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team values engineers who think big, act fast and take responsibility. You will mentor others, raise standards and turn hard system problems into lasting improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Deep experience validating Linux kernels, device drivers or similar systems software&lt;br&gt;· Strong C++ and Python test development skills&lt;br&gt;· Experience with CI/CD, build tools and modern automated testing practices&lt;br&gt;· Ability to

&lt;p class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-start=&quot;135&quot; data-end=&quot;148&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;150&quot; data-end=&quot;240&quot;&gt;Shape how Graphcore products move from hardware design into reliable volume manufacturing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;242&quot; data-end=&quot;471&quot;&gt;As Staff Manufacturing Product Engineer, you will support NPI development and volume production across complex hardware products. You will connect design, test, quality and supply chain decisions with real manufacturing outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;473&quot; data-end=&quot;671&quot;&gt;Your work will help ensure products are manufacturable, resilient and ready for supplier capability. You will provide DfM feedback that improves PCB and system design before issues reach production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;673&quot; data-end=&quot;878&quot;&gt;You will work closely with contract manufacturers, especially during NPI and early volume manufacture. You will drive yield improvement, analyse production data and resolve L6 and L10 manufacturing issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;880&quot; data-end=&quot;1082&quot;&gt;This role suits someone who enjoys practical engineering ownership across design and production. You will travel to Taiwan and work close to suppliers shaping next generation manufacturing technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1084&quot; data-end=&quot;1104&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The team and culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1106&quot; data-end=&quot;1291&quot;&gt;You will join the Manufacturing and Technology Process team within Operations. The team works across Bristol, Cambridge and Taiwan, close to foundry, package assembly and PCBA partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1293&quot; data-end=&quot;1472&quot;&gt;Work happens through clear ownership, supplier engagement and fast feedback into design teams. You will sp

&lt;h1 class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-section-id=&quot;cxqrzp&quot; data-start=&quot;206&quot; data-end=&quot;221&quot;&gt;About the job&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;223&quot; data-end=&quot;296&quot;&gt;Build the test systems that help deliver AI hardware at production scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;298&quot; data-end=&quot;522&quot;&gt;As a Staff Hardware System Test Engineer, you&#39;ll develop manufacturing test solutions for complex compute systems. Your work will help ensure products reach customers with the quality and reliability expected from Graphcore.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;524&quot; data-end=&quot;749&quot;&gt;You&#39;ll shape how hardware is tested across Host Processor Modules, server blades, and multi-node racks. The tools, test content, and diagnostics you create will directly influence manufacturing efficiency and product quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;751&quot; data-end=&quot;978&quot;&gt;You&#39;ll develop test software, design test approaches, and solve challenging hardware issues. You&#39;ll work closely with hardware, firmware, software, and manufacturing teams to improve test coverage and diagnose problems quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;980&quot; data-end=&quot;1236&quot;&gt;This role offers broad technical scope across silicon, boards, systems, software, and manufacturing. You&#39;ll have the opportunity to influence engineering decisions and raise technical standards across the organisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 data-section-id=&quot;80lep1&quot; data-start=&quot;1238&quot; data-end=&quot;1260&quot;&gt;The team and culture&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1262&quot; data-end=&quot;1503&quot;&gt;The Product Test and Diagnosis team owns the strategy for finding and diagnosing hardware defects throughout the product lifecycle. The team works across silicon, boards, servers, and rack-scale systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1505&quot; data-end=&quot;1724&quot;&gt;Day to da

&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot; data-start=&quot;150&quot; data-end=&quot;238&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Build the cloud platform that turns Graphcore AI systems into usable, scalable services.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot; data-start=&quot;240&quot; data-end=&quot;484&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Graphcore needs a Bristol-based Staff Cloud Engineer to develop and deploy private and public cloud services for AI compute. You will join the Cloud Platform team within Software Platform, close to datacentre operations and product development.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot; data-start=&quot;486&quot; data-end=&quot;698&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Your work will shape how internal users and customers access large-scale AI systems. You will keep critical infrastructure available while helping pre-release hardware and software become reliable cloud services.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot; data-start=&quot;700&quot; data-end=&quot;956&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;You will operate and extend OpenStack-based services, automate deployment with infrastructure-as-code, and improve observability across the fleet. You will benchmark, validate and optimise systems spanning Graphcore hardware, servers, switches and storage.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot; data-start=&quot;958&quot; data-end=&quot;1160&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;This role suits someone who wants ownership of hard infrastructure problems, not a narrow ticket queue. Expect unproven components, direct user feedback, and decisions that move quickly into production.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
